# Runtime data. Never commit these -- data/ holds live records including
# password hashes, and uploads/ holds photographs of people's property.
#
# Written as "ignore everything, then name the exceptions", because git will
# not descend into an excluded directory: a bare `data/` makes every !rule
# underneath it dead letter, however correct the rule looks.
data/*
uploads/
instance/

# The exception is geography that came from outside the system. It is source
# data, not runtime records: published barangay coordinates, the coordinates
# the city measured at each MRF, and the raw lists those were read from. No
# personal data, nothing here can regenerate them, and the deploy needs them --
# tools/make_demo_geo.py reads them on boot and falls back to invented
# positions without them, which is how a server ends up showing MRF pins
# several kilometres from the real facilities.
!data/geo/
data/geo/*
!data/geo/barangay_centres.json
!data/geo/mrf_surveyed.json
!data/geo/survey/

# What make_demo_geo.py writes from those stays ignored: regenerated on every
# boot, so committing it would only produce conflicts.
#   data/geo/barangay_zones.geojson
#   data/geo/mrf_locations.json

# Local Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Design source (large images, not needed to run)
# Comment this out if you want the mockups in the repo.
# designs/
